# Both images build with the repository ROOT as context and copy it whole.
#
# The two PACKAGES are deliberately not filtered. `crustify_audit` imports
# `crustify.core`, so excluding either from the other's image breaks it -- a
# partial context fails at import, not at build.
#
# Everything below is either unusable in an image or large enough to slow the
# context transfer. The last entry is the one worth reading twice: `crustify/`
# is anchored at the context root, so it matches the `crustify/audit/` ARTIFACT
# tree a local run would leave here -- not `src/crustify/`, the package, which
# stays. Those artifacts are gitignored but still reach a build context, which
# is why the rule exists at all.
.git/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.egg-info
**/target
crustify/
